       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. At that dose the risks include lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose or frequency.** For example, 500 mg or 1000 mg.\n\nTell me which dose you meant and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
      }
