     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. You've confirmed the dose, but I can't verify that, and no clinical indication supports 5,100 mg/day of metformin. It's twice the labeled maximum, and the main risk is lactic acidosis. Unlike a dose that is only unusually high, this one has no known benefit to offset that risk. Doses above the maximum add little glucose-lowering effect and mostly add toxicity.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Another dose within the labeled range.**\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please do this first:\n1. Discuss it with the clinical pharmacist or the attending.\n2. Document the rationale.\n3. Enter the order through the hospital's override or pharmacy-verification pathway.\n\nI can add a note to a within-range order, such as \"titrate per attending, pharmacy consulted.\""
      }
     ],
